## CORRECTION (2026-10-03, S5 vendor run)

The S2-rest / S4 note above says ARRAY _R goes "column by column on AutoCAD":
that was NOT measured. AutoCAD's run had derailed before the array cases, and
the comparison tool silently skipped records with no value, so an absence read
as agreement. The real AutoCAD answer (job 16915375455) is for -ARRAY:
column by column on AutoCAD -- (0,0) (0,2) (3,0) ... -- while BricsCAD goes row
by row; cador now follows each (it had -ARRAY row by row everywhere). ARRAY _R
on AutoCAD is still unanswered (its ARRAY left the console waiting); column by
column there follows -ARRAY and is marked UNVERIFIED in the code. Lesson kept
in the comparison: a vendor record with no value is MISSING, not equal.

The probe's command check now covers only a list of commands seen absent or
from Express Tools (GETCNAME reported RECTANG unknown), and the S5 cases run
ahead of the arrays, so an array derail cannot take them with it.

## Note: AutoCAD's console and the AutoLISP add-on commands (2026-10-03)

Several core-now commands are not built into AutoCAD but AutoLISP add-ons
loaded on demand: 3DARRAY is 3darray.lsp in the LOCALISED Support folder
(pjb: e.g. '/Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/
Resources/Support/@fr@/3darray.lsp'); C:3DARRAY is an autoload stub. The
CI runner's accoreconsole did not find the file (no localised Support path),
so the stub failed and the probe hung; MATCHPROP is absent from the console
altogether. probe-commands now skips such commands on AutoCAD (BricsCAD
answers them). To measure them on AutoCAD: give the console the localised
Support folder on its search path (a runner setting -- not changed here).

Policy (pjb, 2026-10-03): "We may provide an implementation, notably if
bricscad has one, but if we are able to load autocad's code directly (with
dialect autocad), it's good enough." So for an add-on command, being able to
load and run the vendor's own .lsp under dialect autocad suffices; a native
cador command is optional (3DARRAY has one, as BricsCAD has it built in).
Probe recipe for the console (pjb): (vl-load-com) (load "3darray")
(vlax-add-cmd "3darray" 'c:3darray), then (command "3darray" ...) --
probe-commands follows it on AutoCAD (follow-up MR), finding the file in a
subfolder of the support path when FINDFILE does not.

## S5 confirmed against AutoCAD (2026-10-03, job 16915617788)

The full commands suite ran on AutoCAD 2022's console (54 cases, no hang).
TRIM EXTEND FILLET CHAMFER OFFSET (line, circle) BREAK PEDIT: geometry
identical to clautolisp, as on BricsCAD (job 16914861740 era, 9/9).
OVERKILL: skipped on AutoCAD (Express Tools), BricsCAD-confirmed.
Other differences in that run, none S5:
  - HELIX, REGION: deferred (see S1); MLINE: CMLSCALE (see S1);
  - STRETCH: the console has no view, its crossing window selects nothing;
  - ARRAYRECT: AutoCAD made an ASSOCIATIVE array (INSERT of *U3) despite
    "_AS" "_N"; ARRAYPOLAR left only the source circle -- the probe's input
    sequence does not fit AutoCAD's prompts for these two (UNANSWERED on
    AutoCAD; cador follows BricsCAD's measured answer). To probe: drive
    ARRAYASSOCIATIVITY 0 instead of the _AS option.

## 3DARRAY measured on AutoCAD through its add-on (2026-10-03, job 16915676646)

pjb's recipe works on the console: 3darray.lsp found below the support path,
loaded, C:3DARRAY registered with vlax-add-cmd, (command "3DARRAY" ...) made
the 8 circles. Its ORDER is column by column -- (0,0,0) (0,0,1) (0,1,0) ...
(1,0,0) -- like AutoCAD's -ARRAY, where BricsCAD goes row by row; levels
innermost on both. cador 2.2.165 follows each dialect (!385).

## Phase 4 S6 (hatch / boundary) -- 2026-10-04

Measured first, in two probe rounds (round 1: AutoCAD 16916189663,
BricsCAD macOS 16916189664; round 2: BricsCAD 16916238723, AutoCAD
16916238722). New cador/source/command-hatch.lisp:
  - HATCH / -HATCH: _Properties (name; scale and angle unless SOLID),
    _Select objects (closed LWPOLYLINEs, CIRCLEs), internal points (the
    smallest enclosing boundary), RETURN. Vendor forms per dialect:
    AutoCAD edge loops (92=1; island 92=16 in its own order; a circle one
    arc edge 0..2pi), 75=1, a seed point 98=1 10=0,0,0; BricsCAD polyline
    loops (92=3; island 92=18 walked back from its second vertex; a circle
    two vertices of bulge 1), 75=0, 98=0. Associativity per HPASSOC
    (71, 97, 330 to the source).
  - Patterns: 52 = hatch angle, 53 = line angle + hatch angle (radians);
    each line's base turned by the hatch angle, its offset scaled and
    turned by the line angle. SOLID, ANSI31, ANSI37 measured in both units
    (metric 3.175, imperial 0.125); any other name makes a hatch with no
    pattern lines (to measure, or read from the vendor's .pat file).
  - HATCHEDIT / -HATCHEDIT _Properties; HATCHGENERATEBOUNDARY (a closed
    LWPOLYLINE per loop, hatch made associative -- BricsCAD; AutoCAD 2022's
    console lacks it); BOUNDARY / -BOUNDARY (a closed LWPOLYLINE copy of the
    boundary around each point -- BricsCAD); GRADIENT, SUPERHATCH no-ops.
Against AutoCAD's round 2, every hatch case gives the same groups; the
metric-pattern cases differ only in 45/46 because the vendors' fresh
drawings have MEASUREMENT 1 and cador's 0 (sysvar-template-defaults
question, not changed here).
Open: BricsCAD's -HATCH by internal point made NO hatch in both rounds
(-BOUNDARY at the same point works); cador makes one, as documented.
63 + 19 of 105; 23 to go (S1 SHAPE REGION, S2/S4/S5 remainders).

## Phase 4 remainder: which commands are vendor LISP add-ons (2026-10-04)

pjb (2026-10-03): "We may provide an implementation, notably if bricscad has
one, but if we are able to load autocad's code directly (with dialect
autocad), it's good enough." pjb's recipe for AutoCAD's 3darray.lsp:
(vl-load-com) (load "3darray") (vlax-add-cmd "3darray" 'c:3darray)
(command "3darray" ...).

Measured (BricsCAD V26 macOS, job 16920470455, case "command classes"):
  LISP add-ons on BricsCAD -- its reimplementation of AutoCAD's Express
  Tools: MSTRETCH COPYM NCOPY EXOFFSET BTRIM BEXTEND EXTRIM BREAKLINE MPEDIT
  TREX MOCORO (and SUPERHATCH).
  Built in: 3DROTATE CHSPACE XPLODE UNGROUP ARRAYPATH ARRAYEDIT ARRAYCLOSE
  ARRAYCLASSIC SPLINEDIT HELIX SHAPE REGION.
Driving the LISP ones through COMMAND did nothing on BricsCAD (job
16920411987; EXTRIM's own pick prompt ended the session), so the probe
records them as LISP commands instead of running them.

clautolisp 2.2.170 makes pjb's rule hold: COMMAND runs a C: function
registered with vlax-add-cmd, feeding it the rest of its arguments through
get*, entsel (now real) and ssget, the leftover input going on as further
commands. So the 11 LISP add-ons are covered by loading the vendor's code;
no native cador implementation is planned for them. Native work left: the
12 built-ins (HELIX, REGION, SHAPE deferred as before: vendor spline
approximation, ACIS data, SHX shapes).

AutoCAD 2022's console (job 16920579886, same case): BUILTIN 3DROTATE NCOPY
UNGROUP ARRAYPATH ARRAYEDIT ARRAYCLOSE SPLINEDIT HELIX SHAPE REGION
(3DARRAY: its autoload stub); ABSENT MSTRETCH CHSPACE XPLODE COPYM
ARRAYCLASSIC EXOFFSET BTRIM BEXTEND EXTRIM BREAKLINE MPEDIT TREX MOCORO
FLATTEN OVERKILL SUPERHATCH -- the Express Tools, not loaded by the console
(GETCNAME there has been seen wrong before: indicative). NCOPY is built in
on AutoCAD but a LISP add-on on BricsCAD; CHSPACE / XPLODE / ARRAYCLASSIC
built in on BricsCAD, Express or GUI on AutoCAD.

## The 12 built-ins: inputs from the documentation (2026-10-04)

The prompts were researched in the AutoCAD 2022 help and the BricsCAD
V17/V18/V26 command reference. Findings that shape the probe:
  - XPLODE, CHSPACE, NCOPY are AutoCAD 2022 CORE commands, not Express
    Tools; XPLODE is reported unavailable in the core console. XPLODE's
    "do it" keyword differs: AutoCAD E(xplode), BricsCAD X(plode) -- the old
    "_E" input explains BricsCAD doing nothing; RETURN takes the default on
    both.
  - 3DROTATE on AutoCAD takes its axis by gizmo pick only; BricsCAD's
    accepts X / Y / Z keywords. ROTATE3D is the keyboard form on both.
  - ARRAYCLASSIC is a dialog on both -> a recognised no-op.
  - Deferred: ARRAYEDIT / ARRAYCLOSE (associative arrays, which the
    headless model does not hold; ARRAYEDIT Source and ARRAYCLOSE open
    modal dialogs), CHSPACE (needs a layout with viewports), NCOPY (nested
    picks need a view; a LISP add-on on BricsCAD anyway).
Probe round: XPLODE (BricsCAD), 3DROTATE by keyword (BricsCAD), ROTATE3D,
-GROUP then UNGROUP (the GROUP object reported), ARRAYPATH divide 4
non-associative, SPLINEDIT Reverse / Close.

## Built-ins round 1 -- done (2026-10-04, clautolisp 2.2.171)

Measured (BricsCAD 16920731857, AutoCAD 16920731856) and built in
cador/source/command-builtins.lisp:
  - XPLODE with the defaults = EXPLODE (BricsCAD: 4 LINEs).
  - ROTATE3D (both) / 3DROTATE (BricsCAD, axis keyword): (1,0)-(3,0) 90
    about Z -> (0,1)-(0,3); X / Y / 2-point axes turn the 3D point groups.
  - ARRAYPATH divide 4 non-associative (BricsCAD): the source replaced by
    copies at 0 3 6 9 along the path, listed after it; Measure too; Align
    turns copies along a curved path. AutoCAD did nothing with this input.
  - SPLINEDIT Reverse (BricsCAD; AutoCAD unchanged -- unanswered) and Close
    (IDENTICAL on both: the closed cubic through the fit points and back,
    chord-length clamped knots, equal first and second derivatives at the
    join; 7 control points match to 1e-6; flags + 1 + 2 + 2048, fit data
    dropped).
  - ARRAYCLASSIC: a dialog on both -> recognised.
67 executed + 20 recognised + 11 vendor-LISP of 105. Left: UNGROUP (needs
-GROUP / GROUP objects; the probe's group report failed both times -- fix
the helper, then measure), ARRAYEDIT / ARRAYCLOSE (associative arrays),
CHSPACE (viewports), HELIX / SHAPE / REGION (deferred since S1).

